DTEND:20260807T120000Z
SUMMARY:Choice City Running Festival
DESCRIPTION:A two-day running festival featuring the 28th Annual Jane Welzel Mountain Avenue Mile on August 7th and the 43rd Annual Human Race including a Half Marathon\, 10K\, and 5K on August 8th. Registration opens May 31st.
LOCATION:Civic Center Park\, Fort Collins\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:georgetown-to-idaho-springs-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260808T070000Z
DTEND:20260808T110000Z
SUMMARY:Georgetown to Idaho Springs Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:An iconic point-to-point mountain road race that winds down the Clear Creek Valley. Starting at Georgetown Lake\, the course drops 1\,000 feet in elevation to finish in historic downtown Idaho Springs.
LOCATION:Georgetown Lake\, Georgetown\, CO 80444
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mount-sneffels-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260815T080000Z
DTEND:20260815T120000Z
SUMMARY:Mount Sneffels Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Mt. Sneffels Half Marathon\, 10K\, and Kids Fun Run in the Switzerland of America. All races start and finish at Frontier Field in Ridgway\, CO. Note: Due to county road and bridge construction work\, the half marathon course has been changed and will no longer start in Ouray. Packet pickup is Friday\, August 14th from 4-8 PM at Ridgway Athletic Park/Frontier Field.
LOCATION:Frontier Field\, CR 23\, Ridgway\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-10k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260815T060000Z
DTEND:20260815T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 10K
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 MTB is one of the most prestigious endurance cross-country mountain bike races in the world. Riders tackle a grueling 100-mile course with approximately 12\,000 feet of elevation gain\, reaching peak elevation of 12\,600 feet at Columbine Mine. The race features steep climbs\, technical descents\, and stunning Rocky Mountain scenery. Competitors have 12 hours to complete the race and earn a silver or gold belt buckle.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison Ave\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mt-sneffels-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260815T080000Z
DTEND:20260815T120000Z
SUMMARY:Mt. Sneffels Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Run in the 'Switzerland of America'. The 2026 Mt. Sneffels Half Marathon\, 10K\, and Kids Fun Run will start and finish at Frontier Field in Ridgway due to county road and bridge construction work affecting the original Ouray course. Packet pickup is Friday\, August 14th\, 2026 from 4-8 PM at Ridgway Athletic Park/Frontier Field. The event benefits the Mount Sneffels Education Foundation.
LOCATION:Frontier Field CR 23\, Ridgway\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:staunton-rocks-marathon-and-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260821T070000Z
DTEND:20260821T110000Z
SUMMARY:Staunton Rocks! Marathon and Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:A challenging trail race in Staunton State Park featuring high-altitude singletrack and panoramic mountain views.
LOCATION:Staunton State Park\, 12102 S Elk Creek Rd\, Pine\, CO 80470
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bergen-peak-trail-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T070000Z
DTEND:20260822T110000Z
SUMMARY:Bergen Peak Trail Race
DESCRIPTION:Come run with us in beautiful Evergreen to the top of Bergen Peak at gorgeous Elk Meadow Park! This race day will offer a 5K race running through the lower sections of Elk Meadow Park or a Half Marathon to the top of Bergen Peak. Registration Check-in starts at 6am at the Elk Meadow trailhead access at Buchanan Park Rec Center.
LOCATION:32003 Ellingwood Trail\, Evergreen\, CO 80439
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arrowhead-half-marathon-5k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T070000Z
DTEND:20260822T110000Z
SUMMARY:Arrowhead Half Marathon & 5K
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Vail Trail Running Series
LOCATION:Arrowhead\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T040000Z
DTEND:20260822T080000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 RUN presented by La Sportiva is one of the oldest and most storied endurance running events in the world. This brutal 100-mile out-and-back ultramarathon starts at 10\,200 feet and features over 15\,000 feet of elevation gain with a peak elevation of 12\,500 feet at Hope Pass. Runners compete for coveted silver and gold belt buckles based on finish times under 25 hours (big buckle) or 30 hours (small buckle).
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:staunton-rocks-marathon-half-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T070000Z
DTEND:20260822T110000Z
SUMMARY:Staunton Rocks! Marathon & Half
DESCRIPTION:An event put on by trail runners for trail runners. Touring the renowned singletrack of Staunton State Park in Colorado's Front Range Mountains southwest of Denver. Features flowing trails with gradual climbs & descents\, technical features\, 60+ mile views from overlooks\, scenic lakes and streams\, and wildlife viewing opportunities. Marathon: 4\,500ft elevation gain; Half Marathon: 2\,200ft elevation gain. Elevation range 8\,200'-9\,500'. 90% singletrack\, 10% dirt road. Time allowances: Marathon 10 hours\, Half Marathon 9 hours. Registration caps: 150 per distance.
LOCATION:Staunton State Park\, Pine\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rock-hawk-trail-races-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260829T060000Z
DTEND:20260829T100000Z
SUMMARY:Rock Hawk Trail Races
DESCRIPTION:Rock Hawk Trail Races are held on the gorgeous\, thrilling and rolling trails of Castle Rock's Miller Park & Ridgeline Trail systems. While not overly technical\, these trails will challenge and excite runners while soaking up amazing views. This is an excellent race for both first-time and veteran trail runners\, and provides a nice test for those training for longer summer events. A portion of proceeds benefit open spaces and trails of Castle Rock and partner charities.
LOCATION:Philip S. Miller Park\, 1375 W Plum Creek Pkwy\, Castle Rock\, CO 80109
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:grand-traverse-mountain-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260905T060000Z
DTEND:20260905T100000Z
SUMMARY:Grand Traverse Mountain Run
DESCRIPTION:Point-to-point ultramarathon from Crested Butte to Aspen\, Colorado following the Grand Traverse Backcountry Ski race route. Runners travel 40 miles across the Elk Mountains with over 6\,000 feet of elevation gain. Fundraising event for Crested Butte Nordic\, a 501(c)(3) recreational non-profit organization.
LOCATION:Town Park\, Crested Butte\, CO to Ajax Park – 1001 S. Ute Ave\, Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golden-harvest-half-marathon-5k10k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260905T080000Z
DTEND:20260905T120000Z
SUMMARY:Golden Harvest Half Marathon & 5K/10K
DESCRIPTION:Family-friendly race organized by Bodies Race Company featuring multiple distance options including a Kids Dash. Includes custom race shirt\, finisher medal\, chip-timing with live results\, free photos\, and snacks at the finish line. Age group awards available for 5K/10K/Half Marathon participants. Virtual participation option available.
LOCATION:Parking Lot South of The Westin Westminster\, 10600 Westminster Blvd\, Westminster\, CO 80020
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-grand-traverse-bike-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260906T080000Z
DTEND:20260906T120000Z
SUMMARY:The Grand Traverse (Bike)
DESCRIPTION:The Grand Traverse Bike is a 40-mile point-to-point mountain bike race from Crested Butte to Aspen\, CO. Part of the Grand Traverse Triple Crown series (Ski\, Run\, Bike)\, the race is operated as a fundraising event for Crested Butte Nordic\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit. The route is partially based on historic mail routes connecting the Colorado mining towns of Crested Butte and Aspen from the 1880s. General registration opens at midnight on December 1st.
LOCATION:Crested Butte\, CO to Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
