UID:devil-on-the-divide-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T060000Z
DTEND:20260912T100000Z
SUMMARY:Devil on the Divide
DESCRIPTION:A high-altitude point-to-point trail ultra that stays above 10\,000 feet for nearly the entire distance. The route includes a summit over 13\,000 feet with stunning views of the Continental Divide.
LOCATION:Guanella Pass\, Empire\, CO 80438
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lead-king-loop-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260913T080000Z
DTEND:20260913T120000Z
SUMMARY:Lead King Loop
DESCRIPTION:A spectacular fall running event through peak colors in the heart of the Elk Mountains. The 25K course winds through Lead King Basin\, past the iconic Crystal Mill\, and through the historic Town of Crystal. Also features the 8-Mile Quarry Climb along the Yule Marble Quarry Road. Includes post-race BBQ lunch\, beer (21+)\, custom shirt\, finisher medal\, and kids race. All proceeds benefit Marble Charter School.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-rabbit-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260918T090000Z
DTEND:20260918T130000Z
SUMMARY:Run Rabbit Run
DESCRIPTION:The Run Rabbit Run features two ultramarathon races: the 14th Annual 100 Mile Race on September 18\, 2026 (limited to 450 entrants with Tortoise and Hare divisions) and the 19th Annual 50 Mile Race on September 19\, 2026 (limited to 200 entrants). The 100 mile race offers the highest purse of any 100 mile race with $100\,000 overall ($20\,000 to winners). Registration is currently full; waitlist available. A charity race benefiting northern Colorado nonprofits.
LOCATION:Steamboat Ski Resort\, 2305 Mt Werner Cir\, Steamboat Springs\, CO 80487
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-the-rockies-road-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Run the Rockies Road Race
DESCRIPTION:The 50th Annual Run the Rockies Road race features a downhill course along the Summit County Recreation Path through Ten Mile Canyon. The 11k course (100% downhill) starts at 8:30 AM\, and the Half Marathon course (75% downhill) starts at 8:00 AM. Both races showcase beautiful fall foliage and have a hard stop at 11:30 AM. Registration opens April 22\, 2026. Includes commemorative gifts\, finisher items\, aid stations\, professional timing\, post-race food\, and post-race beer (21+).
LOCATION:Starts near Copper Mountain\, ends at Frisco Historic Park\, 1 Main Street\, Frisco\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ascent-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ascent & Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The oldest continually held marathon in the United States (founded in 1956). The Pikes Peak Marathon takes runners from Manitou Springs to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 grueling mountain miles with approximately 7\,800 vertical feet of elevation gain. The sister race\, the Pikes Peak Ascent\, is a 13.3-mile climb to the summit via the historic Barr Trail.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T070000Z
DTEND:20260920T110000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Known as 'America's Ultimate Challenge\,' this race ascends to the 14\,115-foot summit of Pikes Peak before descending back to Manitou Springs. It is one of the most physically demanding marathons in the world due to the 7\,800-foot vertical climb.
LOCATION:Manitou Ave (City Hall)\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fall-equinox-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T080000Z
DTEND:20260920T120000Z
SUMMARY:Fall Equinox Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Fall Equinox is a multi-day race event held in Fort Collins\, CO\, running from September 20 through October 3\, 2026. It features a Half Marathon and 5 Mile distances.
LOCATION:Fort Collins\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golden-leaf-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DTEND:20260926T120000Z
SUMMARY:Golden Leaf Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Golden Leaf Half Marathon presented by ACG is one of the most beautiful foot races in the Rockies. This 13.3 mile half marathon traverses from Snowmass Village to the heart of Aspen on mountain trails and roads at the height of Colorado's breathtaking fall colors. Chosen by Trail Runner Magazine as one of America's 14 most scenic races and by Colorado Runner as a Best Half Marathon. Registration is SOLD OUT for 2026. Mass start at 8:00 AM with no waves. Requires valid CORSAR card for participation.
LOCATION:Snowmass Village to Aspen\, CO (mountain trails and roads)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cougar-ridge-classic-26k-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T070000Z
