UID:long-view-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261010T073000Z
DTEND:20261010T113000Z
SUMMARY:Long View Marathon
DESCRIPTION:A unique city-to-city trail race running from Fort Collins to Loveland. The marathon course primarily uses the paved Long View and Front Range bike paths\, providing panoramic mountain views and a fast\, net-downhill finish.
LOCATION:Edora Park\, 1420 E Stuart St\, Fort Collins\, CO 80525
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:durango-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261011T080000Z
DTEND:20261011T120000Z
SUMMARY:Durango Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Inaugural Durango Marathon Weekend featuring a scenic road race experience through one of Colorado's most beautiful mountain communities. Starting and finishing at Santa Rita Park along the Animas River\, runners will experience crisp autumn temperatures\, spectacular fall colors\, and sweeping views of the San Juan Mountains. The course begins at approximately 6\,500 feet elevation and reaches nearly 6\,900 feet at its highest point. Race proceeds support the Durango Education Foundation scholarships for local high school students.
LOCATION:Santa Rita Park\, 111 South Camino Del Rio\, Durango\, CO 81301
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blue-sky-marathon-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T070000Z
DTEND:20261017T110000Z
SUMMARY:Blue Sky Marathon & Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Northern Colorado's original trail marathon. The course takes runners on a north-south tour of the easternmost hogbacks of the Front Range on smooth dirt singletrack.
LOCATION:Blue Sky Trailhead\, Horsetooth Mountain Park\, Fort Collins\, CO 80526
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blue-sky-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T080000Z
DTEND:20261017T120000Z
SUMMARY:Blue Sky Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:A scenic trail run taking place on trails between Horsetooth Mountain Park and Devil's Backbone Open Space. The course features 100% dirt terrain with 90% Colorado singletrack\, ranging from smooth dirt trail to technical rock gardens. Marathon course is 26.7 miles (3\,500' elevation gain) with a 9-hour cut-off. Half Marathon is 13.4 miles (1\,800' elevation gain) on October 18\, 2026 with a 6-hour cut-off. Includes aid stations\, finisher awards\, finish line meal\, and gender-specific race t-shirt.
LOCATION:Blue Sky Trailhead\, Horsetooth Mountain Park\, Fort Collins\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bobcat-trail-races-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T070000Z
DTEND:20261017T110000Z
SUMMARY:Bobcat Trail Races
DESCRIPTION:Bobcat Trail Races feature one of Colorado Springs' best city parks\, Palmer Park. Runners will enjoy views of the city and Pikes Peak from the rocky bluffs. The event offers multiple distances (50K\, 25K\, 10K\, 5K) with challenging trail terrain ranging from technical single-track to rolling hills and rocky outcrops. Organized by Aravaipa Running.
LOCATION:Palmer Park\, 3650 Maizeland Rd\, Colorado Springs\, CO 80909
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:all-out-kooky-spooky-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20261101T090000Z
DTEND:20261101T130000Z
SUMMARY:All-Out Kooky-Spooky
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual Kooky-Spooky is a Halloween-themed race featuring a 5K\, 10K\, and half marathon starting from Jefferson County's NAAC Stadium\, winding along the scenic Ralston Creek Trail and by Arvada's Blunn Reservoir. Features a costume contest\, benefits the Colorado National Kidney Foundation\, and serves as an official BOLDERBoulder Qualifier. Virtual options available for all distances.
LOCATION:Ralston Creek Trail\, Golden\, CO 80403
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
